nv-pci: open the PCI sysfs config file against init's root (Linux 7.3)

Since Linux 7.3 ("fs,kthread: start all kthreads in nullfs") a kernel
thread resolves paths in an empty nullfs root instead of sharing init's.
nv_get_pci_sysfs_config() runs in the nv-probe-<bdf> kthread, so its
filp_open() of /sys/bus/pci/devices/<bdf>/config returns -ENOENT,
sysfs_config_file stays NULL, nv_dynamic_power_available() is false and
RTD3 is disabled without an error: the dGPU of a hybrid laptop never
leaves D0. Reported upstream as NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules#1507
against 615.78.08.

Wrap the one lookup in scoped_with_init_fs(), the helper 7.3 added for
kthreads that must open a real path (userspace_init_fs is exported GPL;
the module is Dual MIT/GPL). The file is used through its handle after
this, so nothing else looks up a path. On a kernel without the helper
the macro is undefined and the code is unchanged.

Upstream: not offered; carried
Signed-off-by: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
---
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c	2026-11-02 10:31:02.622839417 -0500
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c	2026-11-02 10:31:11.041063031 -0500
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include "nv-vgpu-vfio-interface.h"
 #endif
 #include <linux/completion.h>
+#include <linux/fs_struct.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/kthread.h>
 
@@ -439,7 +440,21 @@
                    NV_PCI_SLOT_NUMBER(pci_dev));
     if (ret > 0 && ret < sizeof(filename))
     {
-        struct file *file = filp_open(filename, O_RDONLY, 0);
+        struct file *file;
+
+#if defined(scoped_with_init_fs)
+        /*
+         * Since Linux 7.3 a kthread (this runs in nv-probe-<bdf>) resolves
+         * paths in an empty nullfs root, so the sysfs path below is -ENOENT
+         * and RTD3 is silently disabled. Resolve it against init's root, as
+         * in-tree kthreads that open files do. The open file needs no path
+         * lookups after this.
+         */
+        scoped_with_init_fs()
+            file = filp_open(filename, O_RDONLY, 0);
+#else
+        file = filp_open(filename, O_RDONLY, 0);
+#endif
         if (!IS_ERR(file))
         {
 #if defined(NV_SEQ_READ_ITER_PRESENT)
